# Concert Tremolo Etude (repertoire plan: st-concert-tremolo-etude). An original 40-bar tremolo
# study in 3/4, D minor then D major, for p a m i tremolo from the first note to the last.
# Every eighth note is one group of four thirty-second notes: the thumb (p) plays a bass or
# inner note on strings 3 to 6, then a, m and i play the tune note three times on string 1 or 2,
# so the tune seems to sing without a break. The bass at the start of each bar is marked let ring.
# A (bars 1-16, D minor): a falling lament (A | Bb A | G F E | F), then a phrase that climbs to
# F and back to a half close on A; the repeat climbs to G at fret 15 (twelfth position) and
# cadences in D minor. B (bars 17-32, D major): the same tune in major (F becomes F#), then a
# new climb through F#7 and Bm to the top G again, with a borrowed G minor before the cadence.
# Coda (bars 33-40): the opening in major once more, a last B flat from D minor, and a rise to
# a held F# over D major.
# Positions: V (finger 1 on fret 5), IX and X, and XII for the high G. Most shifts happen while
# the thumb plays an open string (A or D), which gives the hand its moment to move. Left-hand
# fingers are marked only at the shifts; p a m i only in bars 1 and 17.
title: Concert Tremolo Etude
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original tremolo study for classical guitar
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 10
tags: tremolo, classical, p a m i, d minor, d major, waltz time, concert
tempo: 63
time: 3/4
key: Dm

track: Your part
